From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 15:19:29 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] xen/swiotlb: translate MMIO resources through the device's
 dma-ranges in map_resource

Under Xen every device in a direct-mapped domain (XENFEAT_direct_mapped:
dom0 and dom0less driver domains with device passthrough) gets
xen_swiotlb_dma_ops, so dma_map_resource() reaches
xen_swiotlb_direct_map_resource() instead of dma_direct_map_phys().

In raspberrypi/linux, dma_direct_map_phys() applies phys_to_dma() to
MMIO addresses as well (372f4e66dad6, "dma-mapping: Use any
dma_range_map for phys to DMA"), i.e. a slave FIFO address is
translated through the DMA master's dma-ranges (dev->dma_range_map).
Mainline does not: its DMA_ATTR_MMIO path uses the physical address as
is. xen_swiotlb_direct_map_resource() returns the CPU physical address
untranslated as well, so on this kernel a device tree "dma-ranges" that
describes a peripheral alias is silently ignored for MMIO targets only
when running as a Xen guest.

Measured on a Raspberry Pi 4 (BCM2711) driver domain: vc4-hdmi audio
programs the DMA40 engine (which sees peripherals at 0x4_7exx_xxxx via
scb's dma-ranges <0x4 0x7c000000  0x0 0xfc000000  0x0 0x3800000>) with
DEST=0x00_fef2001c -- the CPU address of the MAI FIFO -- because the
address came back from dma_map_resource() untranslated.  The transfer
completes at memory speed (2 periods in ~1 ms), the MAI FIFO stays
EMPTY, ALSA reports XRUN every ~100 ms and no sound is produced, all
with error code 0.  The same DTB on bare metal (no Xen, direct ops)
translates correctly.

Use xen_phys_to_dma() here.  For a direct-mapped domain the pfn->bfn
step is the identity for MMIO, so this reduces to phys_to_dma() and the
dma-ranges translation; for a non-direct-mapped domain it is exactly the
bus address the swiotlb-xen page mappings already use.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/xen/swiotlb-xen.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/xen/swiotlb-xen.c b/drivers/xen/swiotlb-xen.c
--- a/drivers/xen/swiotlb-xen.c
+++ b/drivers/xen/swiotlb-xen.c
@@ -398,7 +398,16 @@
 						  enum dma_data_direction dir,
 						  unsigned long attrs)
 {
-	dma_addr_t dma_addr = paddr;
+	/*
+	 * As raspberrypi/linux's dma_direct_map_phys(DMA_ATTR_MMIO) does, put
+	 * an MMIO target through the master's dma-ranges (dev->dma_range_map).
+	 * On a direct-mapped domain xen_phys_to_bus() is the identity for MMIO,
+	 * so this is exactly phys_to_dma(); an untranslated paddr leaves a DT
+	 * dma-ranges peripheral alias silently ineffective under Xen
+	 * (measured: BCM2711 DMA40 -> vc4-hdmi MAI FIFO programmed with the
+	 * CPU address, transfer completes at memory speed, FIFO stays empty).
+	 */
+	dma_addr_t dma_addr = xen_phys_to_dma(dev, paddr);
 
 	if (unlikely(!dma_capable(dev, dma_addr, size, false))) {
 		dev_err_once(dev,
